 ## Background
-Pose Recentering originated in the context of NeRF (Neural Radiance Fields) and LLFF (Look-Lock-Focus) datasets. It addresses the issue that SfM pipelines produce camera poses in an arbitrary coordinate system, which requires normalization for consistent rendering. The specific algorithm described here, often referred to as "LLFF Pose Normalization," is designed to work well with the NDC (Normalized Device Coordinates) system used in many NeRF implementations.
